# NYXUS · earlyoom defaults · rev 2026-08-01
#
# Kill at 5% free RAM / 10% free swap, poll every 60s, notify on kill.
#
# SD-03: earlyoom.service failed on every first boot of the 2026-07-31 image.
# The old value was:
#   EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 60 -n -N --avoid '(...)' --prefer '(...)' -m 5,10 -s 5,10"
# and it was wrong twice.
#
#  1. `-N` takes an argument — it is the script earlyoom runs after a kill. So
#     `-N --avoid` handed earlyoom "--avoid" as the notify script, and the
#     regex that followed became a stray positional argument. earlyoom rejects
#     the command line and exits, which is the whole failure. `-n` alone is
#     what enables notifications.
#
#  2. The single quotes were literal. systemd splits an unquoted $VAR on
#     whitespace without shell-style quote removal, so earlyoom received
#     --avoid with a pattern that had `'` characters baked into it and could
#     never match a real process name. The regexes contain no spaces, so they
#     do not need quoting at all.
#
# The avoid list also still named sddm, which this image has not used since
# the greeter moved to greetd + regreet.
EARLYOOM_ARGS=-r 60 -n --avoid ^(systemd|init|sshd|Hyprland|greetd|regreet|hyprlock)$ --prefer ^(chromium|firefox|electron|node|java|code)$ -m 5,10 -s 5,10
